1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,739
We are Kanishk Sasikumar, Niveth, and
Muhammad. Bearing helps people track

2
00:00:05,739 --> 00:00:12,000
familiar movements on an iPhone and
share personal records with a clinician.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,815
Between visits, remembering routines and
explaining earlier movement can be

4
00:00:16,815 --> 00:00:21,148
difficult. Bearing is intended for
adults tracking familiar exercises,

5
00:00:21,148 --> 00:00:25,000
including older adults and veterans in
rural communities.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,429
Choose from five guided routines, or
create a custom check-in using an

7
00:00:31,429 --> 00:00:36,786
existing routine, timer, or count.
Instructions explain framing and support

8
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:40,000
needs. Manual entries are clearly
labeled.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,375
One challenge was starting without
reaching back to the phone. Tap Start

10
00:00:46,375 --> 00:00:53,812
when ready, then step into view. The app
waits for steady positioning before a

11
00:00:53,812 --> 00:00:57,000
spoken countdown. Recording can be
stopped.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
This synthetic example shows an angle
summary and the attempts that counted.

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The explanation describes the number and
its limits. Comparisons use the same

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
routine, side, and personal starting
point.

15
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,484
The PDF adds ordered attempts when
saved, recording details, matching

16
00:01:17,484 --> 00:01:22,968
history, and personal-plan context.
Missing information is stated instead of

17
00:01:22,968 --> 00:01:29,000
invented. A clinician would still need
medical history and other information.

18
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,774
Users can choose a weekly plan and local
reminder times. The app counts saved

19
00:01:35,774 --> 00:01:40,613
check-ins with recorded values. These
entries show personal tracking, not

20
00:01:40,613 --> 00:01:44,000
proof that every exercise was performed
correctly.

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,179
English, Spanish, larger text, and
voice-speed choices support different

22
00:01:48,179 --> 00:01:54,679
needs. Records stay in the app unless
shared or included in device backups. No

23
00:01:54,679 --> 00:01:57,000
video is saved by Bearing.

24
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,188
Bearing uses Swift, SwiftUI, Apple
Vision, and on-device storage. We worked

25
00:02:03,188 --> 00:02:09,375
together on research, design,
coding, and testing.

26
00:02:09,375 --> 00:02:15,000
The app keeps records on the phone.
Users choose what to share.

27
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,500
One hundred nine unit tests check
movement math, stored records, and

28
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:26,000
report pages. Software tests do not
establish medical accuracy. Device and

29
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
user testing remain important.

30
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,688
A future version could let verified
professionals assign exercise plans,

31
00:02:32,688 --> 00:02:37,844
review shared reports, and update
instructions. That connected loop is not

32
00:02:37,844 --> 00:02:43,000
built yet. It would require consent,
secure access, and professional review.

33
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,500
Bearing brings personal movement records
into one clear, shareable report. Thank

34
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,000
you for watching.
